---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" updated="October 7, 2026">
  <p>
    At Ekwly, we believe in minimal data collection. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect,
    use, and protect your information when you use our bill-splitting and ledger services.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>We only collect the information necessary to provide and improve our services:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account Information:</strong> When you sign in via Google or Email (Magic Link), we
      collect your email address, basic profile name, and profile picture.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Session Data:</strong> We store the names of items, prices, tax presets, and member
      claims within the shared rooms you create or join.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Receipt Images:</strong> When you use the "Magic Scan" feature, the receipt image you
      upload or capture is temporarily processed to extract line items.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How We Process Receipt Images (Magic Scan)</h2>
  <p>
    To provide automated receipt transcription, images are processed using third-party AI services
    (Google Gemini API). <strong>We do not permanently store your receipt images</strong> on our
    servers after the data extraction is complete. The extracted text (items, prices) is saved to
    your session data.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>We utilize trusted third-party infrastructure to run Ekwly:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase:</strong> Used for secure user authentication, database hosting, and
      real-time session synchronization.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google (Gemini API):</strong> Used strictly for Optical Character Recognition (OCR)
      during the Magic Scan process.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. Session data is visible to other users
    who have the exact Room ID and Access PIN for a shared session. Keep your PINs secure.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your Rights & Account Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access, modify, or delete your personal data at any time. You can delete
    your account and wipe your global ledger data directly from the Settings menu inside the Ekwly
    app. Once deleted, this action cannot be undone.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at{' '}
    <strong>support@ekwly.com</strong>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
